<description><![CDATA[Posted November 3, 2015 in response to widespread mis-reporting of a story that bacon gives you cancer. ]]></description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>This was my most popular post. Thats a clue about human nature. </em></p><p><em>My favourite comment was “at last, something useful on LinkedIn”.</em></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg" width="500" height="375" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:375,&quot;width&quot;:500,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:78920,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://compassionaterevenue.substack.com/i/164606316?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7nUZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e3e1245-e414-438d-b142-b843c9b36a5e_500x375.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>There have been many misleading headlines about the risks of bacon recently. As an expert in the risk of Bacon &amp; Egg rolls I thought I should share my occasional reviews, starting with criteria.</p><ol><li><p>The Bacon. It should be streaky and crispy. The big lumpy bits of fat should be trimmed – they are hard to tear out while eating, which causes a risk of collateral damage.</p></li><li><p>The egg. This is where professional chefs can be a real problem. They struggle with application in context: the right egg is not ‘perfectly runny’. It needs to be just hard (flipped briefly) so that yolk doesn’t run down and drip off elbows. Sometimes you need someone who learned on the front-line (e.g. serving out of a caravan window) rather than someone who takes guidance from a book.</p></li><li><p>The Bread – White. Simple as that. No need to be flash, and has to be in proportion to contents or there is a serious risk of a big lump left over at the end with nothing to soak it in.</p></li><li><p>The Sauce – Optional, but never tomato. Maybe a bit of relish, but generally you can’t go past HP. Linked to whether to butter or not. The clear problem here is that some are inclined to load up on extras in the mistaken belief reviewers won’t see it for what it is: unnecessary fat.</p></li><li><p>Construction – this is critical. It must be edible with hands, and without requiring a bib and 20 napkins. It’s kinda the point. If your risk officer insists on cutlery, then you are heading down the wrong path. Risk management should work with marketing requirements, and in this case there is a serious issue: destroying the differentiation with bacon &amp; egg on toast.</p></li></ol><p>And that WHO report? It didn’t say anything like what some headlines blurted, but we all knew that didn’t we?</p>]]></content:encoded>
